      "problem": "Consider the vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ and the block diagonal matrix $B$ shown below, where both $2\\times 2$ blocks of $B$ represent rotation-scaling matrices:\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2-7\\text{i} \\\\ -1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 4+4\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are the eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2+5\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=2\\text{i},$ respectively. \nGiven that $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be the matrix $P?$",
